  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Lady Jane. Logic: See rules.objective and rules.gameplay.',
    Player: 'Lady Jane is a complex two-deck solitaire game belonging to the Spider family. It is characterized by its large tableau of 10 piles and the requirement to build up eight foundations in suit. While it allows building down on the tableau regardless of suit (making it easier to move cards), only same-suit sequences can be moved as a unit, requiring deep tactical planning to keep suits together.',
    objective: 'Move all 104 cards to the eight foundation piles, building up in suit from Ace to King.',
    gameplay: '1. **Foundations**: Build up in suit from Ace to King. Cards are moved individually.\n2. **Tableau**: Build down alternating colors. Cards may be moved individually or as a group if built down in suit. An empty tableau pile may be filled by any exposed card or in-suit sequence from another tableau.\n3. **Stock**: Tap the stock to turn up 3 cards at a time to the waste pile. Only one redeal is allowed.\n4. **Waste**: The top card is available for play onto the tableau or foundations.',
    keyRules: [
      'Foundations: build up in suit from Ace to King; cards moved individually.',
      'Tableau: build down alternating colors; in-suit sequences may move as a unit; empty pile accepts any card or valid sequence.',
      'Stock: tap to turn 3 cards to waste; only one redeal allowed.',
      'Waste: top card is available for play to tableau or foundations.',
    ],
