      players: 'One player only. Lady Jane is a solitaire (patience) game; the player manages the entire layout—ten tableau piles, eight foundations, stock, and waste—making all moves alone.',
      deck: '104 cards (2 standard 52-card decks).',
      equipment: 'Table space for 10 tableau piles, 8 foundation piles, stock and waste.',
      dealing: 'Deal 10 tableau piles: first pile 1 card, second 2, third 3, and so on up to 10 (55 cards total). Place the remaining 49 cards face down as stock. Eight foundation piles and waste start empty.',
    },
    turnFlow: '1. **Foundations**: Build up in suit from Ace to King. Cards are moved individually.\n2. **Tableau**: Build down alternating colors. Cards may be moved individually or as a group if built down in suit. An empty tableau pile may be filled by any exposed card or in-suit sequence from another tableau.\n3. **Stock**: Tap the stock to turn up 3 cards at a time to the waste pile. Only one redeal is allowed.\n4. **Waste**: The top card is available for play onto the tableau or foundations.',
